\f0\fs26 \cf0 I have drawn and painted my whole life, but recently have merged my creative abilities with my love for sewing. What began as exact replications of clothes I love has turned into the ability to create an entire pair of pants, adding practical and aesthetic details as I go. Sewing feels like a hack to consumerism, I can take used sheets, tablecloths, or old clothes and transform them into clothes that I am tempted to buy to refrain from doing so because of the unethical repercussions of overconsumption. Sewing my own clothes forces me to be more conscious about my spending habits and brings a lot more  satisfaction with my wardrobe. }